      "kind" : "declarations"
    },
    {
      "content" : [
        {
          "anchor" : "overview",
          "level" : 2,
          "text" : "Overview",
          "type" : "heading"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "The decoder is designed around a single linear scan through the bytes of the JSON data in order to minimize unnecessary work.",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "This means that elements needs to be decoded in the order the they appear in the JSON data and that to ignore unknown elements in the JSON data,",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "the decoder still needs to parse them to know where that ignored element ends.",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        },
        {
          "inlineContent" : [
            {
              "text" : "The decoder also requires that all keys are static strings known at compile time, and compares their underlying raw bytes.",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "This makes it unsuitable as a general purpose JSON decoder for arbitrary that needs to decode arbitrary structures,",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : " ",
              "type" : "text"
            },
            {
              "text" : "but it’s not an issue for decoding symbol graph data (or even other known structured that are known to use all ASCII keys that don’t require normalization).",
              "type" : "text"
            }
          ],
          "type" : "paragraph"
        }
      ],
      "kind" : "content"
    }
  ],
